CORE
main.c
--show-symbol-table
^  return fma\(x, x, 1\.0\);$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
Invariant check failed
^warning: ignoring
--
The C front end creates __CPROVER_fma's expression with three operands;
adjust_float_expressions adds the rounding mode as the fourth only when the
goto program is built.  Printing the symbol table's value of a function
using it (--show-symbol-table) stopped with "Fused multiply-add must have
four operands"; the expression is now printed with three or four.
